Dear People
I love the reshape and plyr packages, but one thing I cannot get to
work:
(I'm relatively new so my vocabulary may be a bit 'faulty')

a casting formula always needs a list of variables, each typed
separately. ie  cast(df, variable1+variable2+variable3~value,
function)

if the variable name changes between dataset you would have to rewrite
the code.. although they are allways the first second and third column
in the df and therefore can be selected using more generic means...

is there a way to 'construct' the combination  of variables in such a
way that the resulting 'object' can be used in the formula?

so in N00B language something like:

vars <- paste(variable1,"+", variable2, "+", variable3)    (I'm aware
that this doesn't work because you generate a character string, but
can this be converted into something that cast undrstands?)

and then:  cast(df, vars~value, function)

Your help is very much appreciated in advance!!

Thanks
Reen

