Hi,

On Apr 30, 1:13 pm, hadley wickham <h.wick...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Hi Steve,
>
> I think this is a bug in the current version of plyr.  Do you have a
> reproducible example you could send to me off-list so I can test it on
> my machine?

Sure:

I've put up sample code + data you can run:

R> source('http://cbio.mskcc.org/~lianos/hadley/ddply-test.R')
R> load(url('http://cbio.mskcc.org/~lianos/hadley/ddply.data.rda'))

Run it on a small subset of the data so your cpu doesn't explode:

R> rpk <- rpkmFromReadSummary.ddply(summaries[1:1000,], 'cds', TRUE)

I've randomized the data in the counts column so the results might be
wonky, but that's not really relevant to the problem anyway ...

Aso, I'm running R 2.11 (both linux & mac) and plyr_0.1.9

Thanks for taking the time to look into this,

-steve

