> Run it on a small subset of the data so your cpu doesn't explode:
>
> R> rpk <- rpkmFromReadSummary.ddply(summaries[1:1000,], 'cds', TRUE)
>
> I've randomized the data in the counts column so the results might be
> wonky, but that's not really relevant to the problem anyway ...

Old version of plyr:

> system.time(rpk <- rpkmFromReadSummary.ddply(summaries[1:1000,], 'cds', TRUE))
   user  system elapsed
  3.903   0.261   4.202

Development version of plyr:

> system.time(rpk <- rpkmFromReadSummary.ddply(summaries[1:1000,], 'cds', TRUE))
   user  system elapsed
  0.439   0.209   0.658

So it's a big improvement. I'm planning on spending a week or so
optimising plyr even more, so timings should get even better.

